{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CAREGIVER): Sorry, sorry, we're late. Car park was an absolute shocker. And uh his brother rang at breakfast, carrying on about his prostate.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): You're fine, sit down. The brother, did they actually find cancer?",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (CAREGIVER): Prostate cancer, yeah. Told him last month. Look I only booked us in because of that phone call.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. I won't borrow his diagnosis though. What's been bothering you?",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (PATIENT): Up at night.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (DOCTOR): Getting up to the loo. How many times a night?",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (CAREGIVER): Oh it's five, sometimes six. Every night the past month, I hear the floorboards.",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (PATIENT): Three. Four.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (DOCTOR): Three or four, ta, I'll go with you not the counting. Stream a bit weak?",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (PATIENT): Weak.",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (DOCTOR): Mmm. Dribbling after, when you reckon you're finished?",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (CAREGIVER): He does, trousers end up damp and I'm washing them. Um, there was a scratch on his shin off the gate too.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): That scratch, did it heal slowly?",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (CAREGIVER): No. Five days, no trouble.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any blood in the wee?",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (DOCTOR): What are you drinking later on. Tea after dinner?",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (CAREGIVER): Two cups after dinner. Every night. Proper strong.",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (PATIENT): Tea.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (DOCTOR): Err, that late tea will just keep topping the bladder up. High blood pressure still, and you're on amlodipine?",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (DOCTOR): What's your weight, last you knew?",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (PATIENT): Eighty two.",
  "[SEG0025] person_4 (NURSE): Obs while you're talking. Weight is 82 kilograms, same as he said. Blood pressure today is 158 over 94. Chemist slip says amlodipene ten milligrams each morning.",
  "[SEG0026] person_1 (CAREGIVER): No, the dose is five. I do his Webster pack, five milligram tablets, not ten.",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (PATIENT): Five.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): Umm. Slip says ten, you both say five, so I'm not locking a dose in. Does he miss days?",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (CAREGIVER): Sundays. Leaves the Sunday one sitting there.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (PATIENT): Saturday.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (DOCTOR): Saturday, not Sunday. I'm thinking benign prostate enlargement, the gland slowing the outflow, though I can't rule a twitchy bladder out yet.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): So, err, I'll book a PSA blood test and a urine test today.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (DOCTOR): Tamsulosin relaxes the outlet, that's the idea. I'll start it, four hundred micrograms, one capsule at night.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (DOCTOR): We might do a bladder ultrasound if it hasn't settled. Cut the tea after dinner, and I'll see you in three weeks."
 ],
